The void folds open like a dark hand.  
Three cards drift forward, edges glowing.

The first turns face-up: **The High Priestess**, moon-crowned, seated between twin pillars.  
Her gaze locks with yours; a cool tide of knowing lifts behind your eyes, neither urging nor warning—simply watching.

The second card flips: **Six of Cups**, two children sharing brimming goblets beneath a chalk-white arcade.  
Warmth pools in your chest, the scent of rain on old stone streets you swear you have walked.

Last, the **Page of Pentacles** lands upright; a youth lifts a gold coin toward the market lights of an unseen city.  
Your fingertips tingle, as if the stamped disk already rests against your palm.

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.

The void peels away. You draw breath—and wake beneath a real sky, the world waiting to see what you will do with what you carry.

